<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Monitor Redundant Controller Pair and handle any received Switchover Command]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
L_Redun :  REDUNDANT CONTROLLER MONITOR
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib, Cfg_ChasALoc,
Cfg_ChasBLoc; using P_Alarm V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-30:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-02-28:  Conditions for Rdy bits fixed. Added buffering
of Val_Sts, conditioning of Val_Fault.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm V3.1.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This instruction monitors a Redundant Pair of 1756-RM or 1757-SRM Redundancy Modules
and their associated chassis and controlers and provides:

*  Determination if "this" Chassis (the one currently running as Primary) is Chassis A or Chassis B
*  Chassis A and Chassis B Redundancy Module Status
*  Controller A and Controller B Redundancy Status
*  Controller A and Controller B Mode Status (Primary is always "RUN")
*  Controller A and Controller B Keyswitch positions (RUN, REM, PROG)
*   Overall Compatibility Ststus between Chassis A modules and Chassis B modules
*   Synchronization Progress (% complete) between Chassis A and Chassis B
*  Number of data words transferred from Primary RM/SRM to Secondary
(Last = most recent transfer, Max = high water)

*  Optional ability to command a switchover to the Secondary chassis
*  Optional ability to command a disqualified system (set to NOT
auto-qualify) to initiate qualification and synchronization (sync)
(These last two functions provide command busy / done / error status)

IMPORTANT:  Be sure the L_Redun instruction instance is placed in the highest
priority Task. The instruction may show a message error on a commanded
switchover if placed in a Task other than the highest priority Task.
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Cfg_ChasALoc,Cfg_ChasBLoc)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
This rung checks for Configuration errors:

The number of chassis slots is clamped to be between 4 and 17.
If the Alarm Minimum ON Time is invalid, flag an alarm configuration error.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)[LES(Cfg_RackSize,4) MOV(4,Cfg_RackSize) ,GRT(Cfg_RackSize,17) MOV(17,Cfg_RackSize) ,XIC(SecNotRdy.Sts_Err) OTE(Err_Alarm) OTE(Sts_Err) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs handle received Commands:

If the Sync Command is received, clear it.  Then, if Operator Sync Init is allowed
and we're ready (not synced), store the accepted Command for use in logic below.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Sync)OTU(OCmd_Sync)XIC(Cfg_AllowOCmdSync)XIC(Rdy_Sync)OTL(Wrk_Sync)OTU(Sts_SyncDone)OTU(Sts_SyncErr);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the SwitchoverCommand is received, clear it.  Then, if Maintenance Switchover is allowed
and we're ready for a Switchover, store the accepted Command for use in logic below.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Switchover)OTU(MCmd_Switchover)XIC(Cfg_AllowMCmdSwitchover)XIC(Rdy_Switchover)OTL(Wrk_Switchover)OTU(Sts_SwitchoverDone)OTU(Sts_SwitchoverErr);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SYNC REQUEST PROCESSING
============================================================
If a valid sync command has been received, send the appropriate sync
MSG to the 1756-RM / 1757-SRM to initiate synchronization.

This rung sets the tag value to send and the Path to the RM / SRM, then fires the MSG.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Sync)XIC(Wrk_Sync)[MOV(1,Ref_SyncData) ,MOV(2,Ref_SyncMSG.Path.LEN) ,MOV(1,Ref_SyncMSG.Path.DATA[0]) ,GSV(Redundancy,,SRMSlotNumber,Wrk_RMSlot) ,MOV(Wrk_RMSlot,Ref_SyncMSG.Path.DATA[1]) ,MSG(Ref_SyncMSG) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MESSAGE STATUS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
When the MSG completes (DN) or errors out (ER), show the appropriate Status
and clear the request that was latched by the Operator Command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Sync)XIC(Ref_SyncMSG.EN)[XIC(Ref_SyncMSG.DN) OTL(Sts_SyncDone) ,XIC(Ref_SyncMSG.ER) OTL(Sts_SyncErr) ]OTU(Wrk_Sync);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SWITCHOVER REQUEST PROCESSING
============================================================
If a valid switchover has been initiated, configure and send the appropriate
MSG to the 1756-RM / 1757-SRM to initiate the switch.

This rung sets the tag value to send and the Path to the RM / SRM, then fires the MSG.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Switchover)[MOV(1,Ref_SwitchoverData) ,MOV(2,Ref_SwitchoverMSG.Path.LEN) ,MOV(1,Ref_SwitchoverMSG.Path.DATA[0]) ,GSV(Redundancy,,SRMSlotNumber,Wrk_RMSlot) ,MOV(Wrk_RMSlot,Ref_SwitchoverMSG.Path.DATA[1]) ,MSG(Ref_SwitchoverMSG) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MESSAGE STATUS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
When the MSG completes (DN) or errors out (ER), show the appropriate Status
and clear the request that was latched by the Maintenance Command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Switchover)XIC(Ref_SwitchoverMSG.EN)[XIC(Ref_SwitchoverMSG.DN) OTL(Sts_SwitchoverDone) ,XIC(Ref_SwitchoverMSG.ER) OTL(Sts_SwitchoverErr) ]OTU(Wrk_Switchover);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Sync and Switchover DONE and ERROR Status are handled above.
This rung generates the their BUSY Status bits.  It's just our
latched-in Operator Sync or Maintenance Switchover Command (if it was accepted).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Sync) OTE(Sts_SyncBusy) ,XIC(Wrk_Switchover) OTE(Sts_SwitchoverBusy) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND READIES
============================================================
We're Ready to receive the Sync Command if:
*  It is configured to be allowed
* We know where the 1756-RM or 1757-SRM is
*  A sync is not already busy
*  The controllers and chassis are in the right state to accept the request
(PwDS --- so we know we need to start qualification)

#####  V3.0-04:  2014-02-18:  Conditions for Rdy bits fixed.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_AllowOCmdSync)XIO(Wrk_Sync)EQU(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,3)EQU(Wrk_PriChasState,3)OTE(Rdy_Sync);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[We're Ready to receive the Switchover Command if:
*  It is configured to be allowed
* We know where the 1756-RM or 1757-SRM is
*  A switchover is not already busy
*  The controllers and chassis are synchronized
(so we have a backup to switch to!)

#####  V3.0-04:  2014-02-18:  Conditions for Rdy bits fixed.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_AllowMCmdSwitchover)XIO(Wrk_Switchover)EQU(Wrk_SecCtrlrState,8)EQU(Wrk_SecChasState,8)OTE(Rdy_Switchover);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTL(SecNotRdy.PCmd_Ack) ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ]OTL(SecNotRdy.PCmd_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
GATHER REDUNDANCY DATA
============================================================
The following rungs use a series of GSVs to collect data from the 
1756-RM / 1757-SRM redundancy module and from this (primary, running) controller.

First:  Is "THIS" Chassis "A" or B"]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(REDUNDANCY,,PhysicalChassisID,Wrk_PriChassisID);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get THIS chassis and PARTNER chassis "Chassis State".]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(REDUNDANCY,,ChassisRedundancyState,Wrk_PriChasState)GSV(REDUNDANCY,,PartnerChassisRedundancyState,Wrk_SecChasState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get THIS chassis and PARTNER chassis "Controller State".]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(REDUNDANCY,,ModuleRedundancyState,Wrk_PriCtrlrState)GSV(REDUNDANCY,,PartnerModuleRedundancyState,Wrk_SecCtrlrState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get THIS chassis and PARTNER chassis "Controller Keyswitch Position".

Note: for THIS controller, must use the CONTROLLERDEVICE object.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(CONTROLLERDEVICE,,Status,Wrk_PriKeyswitch)GSV(REDUNDANCY,,PartnerKeyswitch,Wrk_SecKeyswitch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get THIS chassis and PARTNER chassis "Controller Minor Fault Status".

Note: for THIS controller, must use the FAULTLOG object.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(FAULTLOG,,MinorFaultBits,Wrk_PriMinorFaults)GSV(REDUNDANCY,,PartnerMinorFaults,Wrk_SecMinorFaults);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get PARTNER chassis "Controller Mode"

Note: for THIS controller to be scanning this code, the Controller Mode must must be "RUN" !!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(REDUNDANCY,,PartnerMode,Wrk_SecCtrlrMode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PUBLISH VALUES AND STATUS
============================================================

One Chassis ID is "1", the other is "2".  "Cfg_Select_A_B"  lets us select which Chassis
reports itself as "Chassis A" and which reports itself as "Chassis B".

By using the Primary Chassis ID and this Configuration selection (which is A, which is B)
in combination (like an XOR), we can show the status of "A is Primary" or "B is Primary".]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_Select_A_B) EQU(Wrk_PriChassisID,1) ,XIO(Cfg_Select_A_B) EQU(Wrk_PriChassisID,2) ]OTE(Sts_PriChassis);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the Qualification Progress value (percent) and the Module CompatibilityCheck.

NOTE: The percent complete is "-1" before qualification occurs!
THEN it goes from 0 to 100, staying at 100 when secondary qualification completes.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(REDUNDANCY,,QualificationInProgress,Val_QualProgress)GSV(REDUNDANCY,,CompatibilityResults,Val_Compat);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get Primary to Secondary DATA TRANSFER STATISTICS

The GSVs get the Last (most recent) and High Water (largest amount since powerup/reset)
number of data words (DWORDs, 32-bit) transferred from Primary to Secondary.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(REDUNDANCY,,LastDataTransferSize,Val_XferSizeLast)GSV(REDUNDANCY,,MaxDataTransferSize,Val_XferSizeMax);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Primary controller (the one running the code) is Chassis "A", put the data for
the Primary chassis and controller in the "A" chassis / controller Status and Values, and the data
for the Secondary chassis and controller in the "B" chassis / controller Status amd Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_PriChassis)[MOV(Wrk_PriChasState,Val_ChasStateA) MOV(Wrk_SecChasState,Val_ChasStateB) ,MOV(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,Val_CtrlrStateA) MOV(Wrk_SecCtrlrState,Val_CtrlrStateB) ,BTD(Wrk_PriKeyswitch,12,Val_KeyswitchA,0,2) MOV(Wrk_SecKeyswitch,Val_KeyswitchB) ,MOV(Wrk_PriMinorFaults,Val_MinorFaultsA) MOV(Wrk_SecMinorFaults,Val_MinorFaultsB) ,MOV(2,Val_CtrlrModeA) MOV(Wrk_SecCtrlrMode,Val_CtrlrModeB) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If this controller (primary, running the code) is Chassis "B", put the data for
"THIS" chassis and controller in the "B" chassis / controller Status and Values, and the data
for the "OTHER" chassis and controller in the "A" chassis / controller Status amd Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_PriChassis)[MOV(Wrk_PriChasState,Val_ChasStateB) MOV(Wrk_SecChasState,Val_ChasStateA) ,MOV(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,Val_CtrlrStateB) MOV(Wrk_SecCtrlrState,Val_CtrlrStateA) ,BTD(Wrk_PriKeyswitch,12,Val_KeyswitchB,0,2) MOV(Wrk_SecKeyswitch,Val_KeyswitchA) ,MOV(Wrk_PriMinorFaults,Val_MinorFaultsB) MOV(Wrk_SecMinorFaults,Val_MinorFaultsA) ,MOV(2,Val_CtrlrModeB) MOV(Wrk_SecCtrlrMode,Val_CtrlrModeA) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,2) ,NEQ(Wrk_SecCtrlrState,8) ,NEQ(Wrk_PriChasState,2) ,NEQ(Wrk_SecChasState,8) ]OTE(Sts_SecNotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
This rung generates the enumerated Redundancy Status:
0 = Unknown
1 = Synchronized, ready for Secondary to take over
2 = Synchronizing
3 = Primary with Disqualified / Not Ready Secondary
4 = Primary with NO Secondary Present

And this rung generates the enumerated Redundancy Fault Status:
0 = none
16 = Secondary is Not Ready to take over (not synchronized or not qualified or not present)
17 = Error communicating with Redundancy Module

#####  V3.0-04  2014-02-19:  Added buffering of Val_Sts, modified conditioning of Val_Fault.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) ,XIO(Sts_SecNotRdy) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ,[EQU(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,6) ,EQU(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,7) ] MOV(2,Wrk_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,3) MOV(3,Wrk_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_PriCtrlrState,4) MOV(4,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_SecNotRdy) ONS(Wrk_SecNotRdyONS) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIO(Sts_SecNotRdy) ONS(Wrk_SecRdyONS) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,[XIC(Ref_SwitchoverMSG.ER) ONS(Wrk_SwoverMsgErrONS) ,XIC(Ref_SyncMSG.ER) ONS(Wrk_SyncMsgErrONS) ] MOV(17,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(SecNotRdy.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Secondary Not Ready alarm is ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(SecNotRdy.PCfg_AllowExist);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(SecNotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SecNotRdy.Sts_AlmInh)OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(SecNotRdy.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(SecNotRdy.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,XIC(SecNotRdy.Val_Notify.0) OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(SecNotRdy.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(SecNotRdy.Rdy_Reset) OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear any "lurking" Switchover command and related status]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, clear all Command Ready and latched internal
bits related to the Sync and Switchover Commands.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Rdy_Sync)OTU(Wrk_Sync)OTU(Rdy_Switchover)OTU(Wrk_Switchover);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear any "lurking" commands.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(OCmd_Sync)OTU(MCmd_Switchover)OTU(OCmd_Reset)OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll)OTU(PCmd_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear Command Status bits]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Sts_SyncBusy)OTU(Sts_SyncDone)OTU(Sts_SyncErr)OTU(Sts_SwitchoverBusy)OTU(Sts_SwitchoverDone)OTU(Sts_SwitchoverErr);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
<ControllerDevice Use="Reference">
</ControllerDevice>
<FaultLog Use="Reference">
</FaultLog>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
